actually creates a better growth

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:13.360
environment for my hair. It's been very

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:15.800
thoroughly researched that your scalp

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:17.760
hygiene directly impacts your hair

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:20.240
growth. Tip number six, check your

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.160
water. This one is huge and I don't

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:24.760
really hear people talking about this.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:27.200
Hard water deposits calcium and

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:28.920
magnesium onto your hair and the

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:31.200
minerals prevent your conditioner from

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:33.640
actually binding to your strands. They

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:35.800
increase friction, they cause dullness

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:37.760
and tangling. So if you live in an old

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:39.360
building with aging pipes it's probably

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:42.320
even worse. Back when I used to live in

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:44.080
New York the water pipes were horrible

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:46.160
because my building is really old and

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:48.560
old buildings especially in older cities

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.520
is super common. It made such a

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:52.560
difference in my hair and not in a good

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:54.880
way. This might sound weird but I tend

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:57.520
to notice the hard water especially in

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:59.600
cities where the water supply has to

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.120
travel a really long way and it

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:04.760
basically collects sediments along the

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:06.480
way all the way into your shower.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:10.000
there's some cities that have amazing

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:11.440
water like Tokyo for example, Istanbul.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.400
When I was in Bulgaria the water was

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.560
amazing but the chances are if you're in

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.240
an old building that hasn't been

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:18.480
renovated for a long time you might

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:21.080
benefit from this fix. And the solution

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:23.200
is simple, just install a shower filter

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:25.320
and replace it every six months. I get

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:28.000
mine from Amazon, it costs about 20 to

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:29.600
30 dollars and this alone can completely

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.440
transform your hair, I'm not even

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:33.840
kidding. Tip number seven, apply

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:36.920
products the right way. Always start at

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:40.000
the ends and then work your way upwards.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:42.320
Never pile product on your scalp. Why is

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:45.000
that? Your ends are the oldest and the

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:47.360
most damaged part of your hair. They

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:49.760
need the most attention. Your scalp does

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:52.000
not need to be coated in conditioner.

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:55.480
That just causes follicle congestion and

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:58.040
build-up and limp roots. So, whenever I

00:11:55.480 --> 00:12:00.320
apply conditioner, treatment, serums,

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:03.800
anything like that, I always start from

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:06.040
the ends first and then work my way up.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:08.200
I'm always making sure that my ends are

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:10.400
moisturized first and this rule is

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:13.040
completely non-negotiable. And as for

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:15.480
serums, I use a silicone hair serum from

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:17.840
YesStyle. I find that Japanese silicone

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:20.240
hair products specifically are the

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:22.240
absolute goat. I'm also a huge fan of

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:23.760
Japanese hair styling products. I just

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.000
don't find them to be as damaging to the

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:28.640
hair. Tip number eight, use two brushes.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:30.880
I use a detangling brush and a boar

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:33.000
bristle brush and they serve different

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:36.000
purposes. So, the detangling brush

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.960
prevents mechanical breakage on wet or

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.800
fragile hair. Some of you may be

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:41.400
surprised that I brush my hair while

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:43.560
it's wet. Most people say that you're

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:45.560
not supposed to, but not if you use a

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:47.800
detangling brush specifically built for

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:50.240
that. And then the boar bristle brush

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:52.400
distributes your natural sebum from your

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.720
scalp to your ends. It smooths the

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:56.480
cuticle and enhances shine without

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:58.600
adding more product. Basically, that

00:12:56.480 --> 00:13:00.200
means if you start combing from the root

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:02.680
of your hair with a boar bristle

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:04.760
hairbrush and you comb all the way down,

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:06.440
you're basically spreading the natural

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:08.480
oils of your hair. So, you don't even

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:10.600
need to use that much hair product. But

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:12.680
I also use this to spread my hair

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:14.800
products evenly and to distribute the

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:17.200
moisture from top to bottom. Always

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:20.080
making sure that my tip is getting what

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:21.560
it needs. Sometimes I use them both in

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:24.200
the same session, but basically my

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:26.320
routine is detangle first and then

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.960
finish off with a boar bristle to polish

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.880
it off and your hair is going to look

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:32.600
completely different. Tip number nine,

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:35.160
scalp care is everything. Your scalp

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:36.680
health controls everything downstream.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:39.320
So, if your scalp is congested,

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:41.680
inflamed, or clogged, or flaky, your

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:43.640
hair cannot thrive. I wash it

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:44.960
frequently, especially in humid weather,

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:47.360
because otherwise my hair starts getting

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:49.880
really gross, and I use a silicone scalp

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:52.800
massager twice a day, once in the

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:55.000
mornings, and once whenever I shower.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:57.480
When I shampoo, I use the massager to

00:13:55.000 --> 00:14:00.120
really clean my scalp and get all of the

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.920
buildup out. Scalp massagers also

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:04.240
improve circulation, which helps your

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:06.960
hair grow. It helps products penetrate

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:09.040
better, and it also reduces all of the

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:11.360
sebum that's up here. There's also

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:14.000
actually research showing that scalp

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:16.200
massage can increase hair thickness.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:18.840
This is such a simple practice, but most

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:20.920
people skip it. A scalp massager only

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.320
costs a couple of bucks, and I'm telling

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:25.080
you this little tool makes a huge

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:27.040
difference. Tip number 10, minoxidil for

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:29.120
hairline density. So, this one is

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:30.760
optional and definitely not necessary

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:32.360
for everyone, but I still want to share

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:35.480
it anyway because it helps thicken my

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:38.080
hair. I use 5% minoxidil. You can get it

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:40.200
on Amazon as well. I started using it

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:42.200
because I wanted to fill in the sides of

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:45.040
my hairline, where it was looking a

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:47.720
little sparse. And after about 8 months

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:49.920
of applying it almost every day, I have

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:52.160
baby hairs growing now, where there

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:54.560
weren't baby hairs before, which is

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:56.440
crazy. So, this does take a while, but

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:59.200
at least I don't have to fly to Turkey,

00:14:56.440 --> 00:15:01.240
right? Minoxidil was originally a blood

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:03.120
pressure medication, and they discovered

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:05.800
that it also stimulates hair growth as a

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:07.800
side effect. It increases blood flow to

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:09.960
the follicles, and it also extends the

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:12.240
growth phase of your hair cycle. It is

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:14.120
FDA approved, and the thing is, you have

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:16.760
to be consistent about it. If you stop

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:19.520
using it, the new growth can actually

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:22.240
fall out. So, it's a commitment. I apply

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:24.920
it to my scalp in the mornings and let

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:27.120
it just dry and that's it. Totally

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:29.160
optional, but it's something that I do.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:31.520
Your hair can be healthy and beautiful

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:33.720
without this, but if thinning edges or

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:35.800
sparse hairline bothers you, this

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:37.720
actually has some science and research

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:39.600
behind it. Tip number 11, getting the

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:41.840
right haircut. This matters more than

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:44.000
most people think. For low porosity

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:47.880
straight hair, the best cuts are blunt

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:50.600
cuts, soft U shapes, or long layers with

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:53.480
minimal texturing. I get micro trims

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:56.320
every few months, not even. And I also

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:59.000
do it myself. But what you want to avoid

00:15:56.320 --> 00:16:01.680
is razor cuts, over thinning your hair,

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:03.640
and excessive feathering. These destroy

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:06.000
the illusion of density. Your hair will

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:07.840
look thinner, even if it's not. Unless

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:10.160
you're going for the wolf cut and you're

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:11.120
willing to style it frequently, and I

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.960
know that the wolf cut is really

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:15.880
popular. You can also benefit from

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:17.880
finding a stylist who understands that

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:20.880
style and also understands your hair.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:23.200
Because one bad haircut can set you back

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:25.480
for months. So, all of these things are

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:28.040
what I do and it's the truth that silky

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:30.800
hair is maintained. It is chemistry,

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:33.640
water quality, friction control, and

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:35.440
consistency. If I didn't do like five of

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:37.080
those steps, I would not have this hair.

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:38.960
Pretty hair is intentional. You don't

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:40.160
need good genes or spend a lot of money

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:42.200
to get it. All you have to do is

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:43.920
understand the science and be consistent

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:45.680
about it. That's it. I literally went

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:48.560
from a fried bleach bob that wouldn't

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:50.680
grow past my chin to butt length healthy

